- From RFC3530 (bibliographic) → `orphan/RFC3530/h:208a562d`:
  - cite: Juszczak, Chet, "Improving the Performance and Correctness of an NFS Server," USENIX Conference Proceedings, USENIX Association, Berkeley, CA, June 1990, pages 53-63. Describes reply cache implementation that avoids work in the server by handling duplicate requests. More important, though listed as a side-effect, the reply cache aids in the avoidance of destructive non- idempotent operation re-application -- improving correctness.
